    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d167">

                <pb facs="0171" n="121" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg121"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.61323/–</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Moscow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Summers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-04-25T19:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 25, 1918,
                                7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department has telegraphed Embassy Vologda recommending purchase flax referred to
                    your 338, April 11, 4 p.m. Military attaché was granted authority in February to
                    draw for $1,000,000 for this or similar purposes.</p>
                <p>Communicate with Embassy and cable Department result.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
